# Mysterio, Master of Illusion ({3}{U}): "When Mysterio enters, create a 3/3 blue Illusion Villain creature token for each nontoken
# Villain you control" (CR 111.1, 608.2c). Turn 1: Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire pay for him; he is the only Villain Bot1 controls,
# so one token, though Bot2's Mysterio's Phantasm (turn 2, a Villain too) is not Bot1's to count. Turn 3: Chameleon, Master of
# Disguise (a Villain) enters as a copy of Mysterio, so his enter trigger runs again: the nontoken Villains are the two of them,
# and the Illusion Villain token already there (a Villain, but a token) is not counted: two more tokens, three in all.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mysterio, Master of Illusion
Chameleon, Master of Disguise
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
